**5. Citation errors in the mechanical-basis column.** Item 1 cites `CONTRACT_TEST_PROFILE_V1.md` §1.5 and §1.6; §1.5 covers only `ResourceCeiling`, §1.6 only TypeDef invariants. `EffectBound` and `CapabilityBound` are rejected by §1.1's table and the preamble, neither cited. Item 3d cites §3.3; the replay-scope and adapter-configuration text is §3.2, which says those *must* be defined — the policy softens it to "may define". Item 3b borrows §1.1's anti-reinterpretation clause, which is scoped to ContractKind tags, and applies it to `test_observe`; correct support is §3.4 plus the preamble.

**6. Item 2 is the only determination with no contract citation, and its terms don't resolve.** "Optional field 4 of the frozen epoch-1 descriptor" matches no descriptor in `SCHEMA_EPOCH_V1.md`: record field 4 is `unicode_nfc_version`, `ContractDescriptor` 4 is `field_schema_hash`, `MigrationContractDescriptor` 4 is `scope_hash`, `ExtensionDescriptor` 4 is `payload_schema_hash` — all required. `full_v1` exists only as `CandidateValidationLimits::full_v1()` in code and appears in no spec document.

**7. Checker/staging coupling.** `SPEC_MARKERS` pins the literal `"Status: S20-760 contract draft, revision 2"`, so §8's own `S20_760_POLICY_ACCEPTED` transition, and any revision 3, fail the checker. `ADR_MARKERS` omit decision 6 ("A determination is not an approval") — the revision-2 addition that licenses §6 could be deleted and the checker still passes.

